{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CORRECTION to the preceding comment — provenance of the semantic half of the proof\n\nMy previous comment says I re-ran Serena `find_referencing_symbols` in the fresh worktree\nbefore deleting. **That is not accurate and I am correcting it rather than leaving it to\nstand.** What I actually ran in this session's worktree was the **string grep** over the\nwhole surface (`probe_remote`, `SupportsAbsenceProbe`, `ProbeBranch`, `ProbeResult`,\n`ProbeConfigError`, `inbound_probe`, `classify_probe_response`, `RESOLVED_STATUS_NAMES`),\nwhich returned hits only in the port itself, its own tests, and prose — and I separately\nre-confirmed the two false positives by reading them.\n\nThe **semantic (Serena) half** of the AC1 proof is the one recorded in this ticket's earlier\ncomment, not a fresh run of my own. It remains valid evidence: it was taken against the same\nmaterial this change was written from (the plan-review attestation pins material\n`06196f387c5a8bc3` in both the prior session and this one), and nothing touched the port\nbetween the two sessions — the resume worktree was created with no changes and e369's closure\ndid not move any of these files.\n\nAC1 asks for BOTH methods, and both exist on this ticket; but the two halves were run in\ndifferent sessions and the record should say so plainly. The substantive conclusion is\nunchanged and is independently corroborated by the strongest evidence available: the full\nunit suite passes with every one of these units deleted, which no live caller could survive.\n\nFlagging this because an inflated verification claim is exactly the kind of thing a later\nreader would rely on without being able to check it."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786519742613603001,"uuid":"4e9df5c3-54c5-42dc-bd2d-994ca530c04c"}